WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.133
Welcome to Module 4 of the
Microsoft Automation learning path:

2
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:08.138
Azure Arc through Azure Resource
Manager and Resource Graph.

3
00:00:08.138 --> 00:00:13.295
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Devices and Endpoints book puts the agency's

4
00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:16.435
servers under Azure Arc,
and its Data Platform book

5
00:00:16.435 --> 00:00:19.949
uses Arc to bring SQL Server
under Microsoft Entra I D.

6
00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:23.113
After onboarding, the
question becomes evidence.

7
00:00:23.113 --> 00:00:25.388
None of that is in Microsoft Graph.

8
00:00:25.388 --> 00:00:27.277
Arc servers, their extensions,

9
00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:32.265
SQL Server instances and Azure Policy
are Azure resources, managed through

10
00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.649
Azure Resource Manager and read in
bulk through Azure Resource Graph.

11
00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:40.800
In this module you'll learn what
changes when a script leaves Graph for

12
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.450
Resource Manager, and how to read Resource
Graph without silently losing rows.

13
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.862
Then you'll run five read-only checks,

14
00:00:47.862 --> 00:00:51.400
in Python and PowerShell,
against a fictional estate.

15
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.609
Like the other modules'
checks, they're illustrative:

16
00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.990
unit-tested against fixtures, not
proven against live subscriptions.
